# TrafficRL Project — Stage-by-Stage Evolution

A complete walkthrough of the project's development from a single-intersection DQN prototype to a fine-tuned multi-junction real-world corridor controller.

---

## Overview of Stages

| Stage | Name | Environment | Agent | Training Episodes |
|-------|------|-------------|-------|-------------------|
| 1 | **Basic DQN** | Single 4-way intersection | Standard DQN (128×128) | 200 |
| 2 | **Multi-Head DQN** | Single 4-way intersection | Multi-Head DQN (3 regime heads) | 200 |
| 3 | **Grid Network** | 3×3 grid (9 intersections) | Multi-Head DQN (per-junction) | 200 |
| 4 | **Habsiguda Corridor** | 6-junction real-world corridor | Transfer from pre-trained model | 100 |
| 5 | **Fine-Tuned Model** | 6-junction corridor (tuned penalties) | Fine-tuned Multi-Head DQN | 100 |

---

## Stage 1 — Basic DQN (Single Intersection)

### Environment Snapshot

```mermaid
graph TD
    N["North Approach"] --> C["4-Way Intersection<br/>(TL Controlled)"]
    S["South Approach"] --> C
    E["East Approach"] --> C
    W["West Approach"] --> C
    C --> N2["North Exit"]
    C --> S2["South Exit"]
    C --> E2["East Exit"]
    C --> W2["West Exit"]

    style C fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
    style N fill:#3498db,stroke:#2980b9,color:#fff
    style S fill:#3498db,stroke:#2980b9,color:#fff
    style E fill:#2ecc71,stroke:#27ae60,color:#fff
    style W fill:#2ecc71,stroke:#27ae60,color:#fff
```

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Network** | [network.net.xml](file:///e:/github_projects/trafficRL/traffic_rl/sumo/network.net.xml) (simple 4-way) |
| **State Space** | 9-dim: [queue_N, queue_S, queue_E, queue_W, wait_N, wait_S, wait_E, wait_W, phase] |
| **Action Space** | 2 actions: NS green / EW green |
| **Reward** | `-0.1×wait - 0.1×queue + 1.0×throughput - 0.05×phase_change` |
| **Architecture** | DQN: Input(9) → FC(128) → FC(128) → Output(2) |
| **Training** | 200 episodes, ε: 1.0→0.05, LR: 0.0001, γ: 0.99 |
| **Traffic** | 1850 vehicles/episode, balanced distribution |

### Results — Stage 1

![Training curves from the base DQN model](C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity/brain/58539d9e-98a7-4db9-abeb-cef76220d619/training_curves_main.png)

![DQN vs Fixed-Time Baseline comparison](C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity/brain/58539d9e-98a7-4db9-abeb-cef76220d619/dqn_vs_baseline.png)

> [!NOTE]
> The basic DQN served as a proof-of-concept, establishing the RL pipeline and reward function design. Training curves show learning over 200 episodes. The fixed-time baseline uses 30s NS green + 30s EW green cycles.

---

## Stage 2 — Multi-Head DQN (Single Intersection, 3 Regime Heads)

### Environment Snapshot

The same single 4-way intersection is used, but the agent architecture changes significantly:

```mermaid
graph LR
    S["State (9-dim)"] --> E["Shared Encoder<br/>256 → 256"]
    E --> H1["Q-Head 1<br/>(Low Traffic)<br/>128 → 2"]
    E --> H2["Q-Head 2<br/>(Medium Traffic)<br/>128 → 2"]
    E --> H3["Q-Head 3<br/>(High Traffic)<br/>128 → 2"]
    E --> RC["Regime Classifier<br/>128 → 64 → 3"]
    RC -->|"soft gating"| G["Gated Q-Values"]
    H1 --> G
    H2 --> G
    H3 --> G

    style S fill:#9b59b6,stroke:#8e44ad,color:#fff
    style E fill:#3498db,stroke:#2980b9,color:#fff
    style H1 fill:#2ecc71,stroke:#27ae60,color:#fff
    style H2 fill:#f39c12,stroke:#e67e22,color:#fff
    style H3 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
    style RC fill:#1abc9c,stroke:#16a085,color:#fff
    style G fill:#34495e,stroke:#2c3e50,color:#fff
```

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Regime Thresholds** | Low: queue ≤ 3, wait ≤ 10s · Medium: queue ≤ 8, wait ≤ 25s · High: above |
| **Gating** | Soft (weighted mixture of all heads) |
| **Classifier Loss Weight** | 0.1 |
| **Training** | 200 episodes, same intersection |

### Results — Stage 2

| Metric | Multi-Head DQN | Fixed-Time Baseline | Improvement |
|--------|---------------|--------------------:|------------|
| **Avg Waiting Time (s)** | 0.24 ± 0.01 | 0.92 | **+73.9% ↓** |
| **Avg Queue Length** | 2.17 ± 0.12 | 3.79 | **+42.7% ↓** |
| **Throughput (veh/h)** | 1132.5 ± 12.9 | 1297.0 | -12.7% |
| **Avg Reward** | 1098.9 ± 13.0 | 1253.5 | -12.3% |
| **Phase Changes** | 252.9 | 109.0 | +132% more switching |

![Multi-Head DQN performance comparison bar charts](C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity/brain/58539d9e-98a7-4db9-abeb-cef76220d619/multihead_vs_baseline.png)

![Per-episode comparison of Multi-Head DQN vs Fixed-Time](C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity/brain/58539d9e-98a7-4db9-abeb-cef76220d619/episode_comparison.png)

````carousel
![Multi-Head DQN training metrics over 200 episodes](C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity/brain/58539d9e-98a7-4db9-abeb-cef76220d619/multihead_training_metrics.png)
<!-- slide -->
![Head specialization across traffic regimes](C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity/brain/58539d9e-98a7-4db9-abeb-cef76220d619/head_specialization.png)
<!-- slide -->
![Regime distribution during training](C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity/brain/58539d9e-98a7-4db9-abeb-cef76220d619/regime_distribution.png)
<!-- slide -->
![Regime confusion matrix](C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity/brain/58539d9e-98a7-4db9-abeb-cef76220d619/regime_confusion_matrix_multihead.png)
````

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The Multi-Head DQN dramatically reduced waiting times (73.9%) and queue lengths (42.7%) compared to fixed-time. However, throughput dropped 12.7% because the agent traded vehicle completion for lower congestion. More frequent phase switching (253 vs 109) shows the agent actively adapting.

