## Stage 3 — Grid Network (3×3, 9 Intersections)

### Environment Snapshot

```mermaid
graph TD
    I00["Intersection<br/>(0,0)"] --- I01["Intersection<br/>(0,1)"] --- I02["Intersection<br/>(0,2)"]
    I10["Intersection<br/>(1,0)"] --- I11["Intersection<br/>(1,1)"] --- I12["Intersection<br/>(1,2)"]
    I20["Intersection<br/>(2,0)"] --- I21["Intersection<br/>(2,1)"] --- I22["Intersection<br/>(2,2)"]
    I00 --- I10 --- I20
    I01 --- I11 --- I21
    I02 --- I12 --- I22

    style I00 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
    style I01 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
    style I02 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
    style I10 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
    style I11 fill:#f39c12,stroke:#e67e22,color:#fff
    style I12 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
    style I20 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
    style I21 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
    style I22 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
```

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Network** | [grid_network.net.xml](file:///e:/github_projects/trafficRL/traffic_rl/sumo/grid_network.net.xml) (3×3 grid) |
| **Intersections** | 9 signalized junctions |
| **Per-Junction State** | 9-dim (same as single intersection) |
| **Per-Junction Action** | 2 actions: NS green / EW green |
| **Agent** | Multi-Head DQN shared across all junctions |
| **Training** | 200 episodes, coordination score tracked (all 0.0) |
| **Env Class** | [GridSUMOEnv](file:///e:/github_projects/trafficRL/traffic_rl/env/grid_sumo_env.py#23-440) (multi-agent step) |

### Results — Stage 3

| Metric | Early (Ep 1-10) | Mid (Ep 100) | Late (Ep 190-200) | Trend |
|--------|---------------:|-------------:|------------------:|-------|
| **Avg Reward** | -565.7 | -503.7 | -485.3 | ↑ +14.2% |
| **Throughput (veh/h)** | 467.2 | 473.9 | 487.3 | ↑ +4.3% |
| **Best Reward** | — | — | **-441.5** (Ep 113) | — |
| **Worst Reward** | **-628.7** (Ep 1) | — | — | — |

> [!TIP]
> Training reward improved from approximately -629 → -441 over 200 episodes, demonstrating learning across the 9-junction grid. Throughput also gradually increased. Coordination scores remained at 0.0, suggesting junctions operated independently without explicit coordination.

