## Cross-Stage Comparison Tables

### Waiting Time Reduction vs Fixed-Time Baseline

| Stage | Avg Waiting Time (RL) | Avg Waiting Time (Baseline) | Reduction |
|-------|---------------------:|---------------------------:|-----------|
| 2 — Multi-Head DQN (single) | 0.24 s | 0.92 s | **73.9%** |
| 4 — Habsiguda (original) | 1.57 s | 3.11 s | **49.5%** |
| 5 — Habsiguda (fine-tuned) | 1.86 s | 3.11 s | **40.2%** |

### Throughput vs Fixed-Time Baseline

| Stage | Throughput (RL) | Throughput (Baseline) | Gap |
|-------|---------------:|---------------------:|-----|
| 2 — Multi-Head DQN (single) | 1132.5 veh/h | 1297.0 veh/h | -12.7% |
| 4 — Habsiguda (original) | 633.3 veh/h | 945.5 veh/h | -33.0% |
| 5 — Habsiguda (fine-tuned) | 824.4 veh/h | 926.7 veh/h | **-11.0%** |

### Queue Length Reduction

| Stage | Avg Queue (RL) | Avg Queue (Baseline) | Reduction |
|-------|---------------:|--------------------:|-----------|
| 2 — Multi-Head DQN (single) | 2.17 | 3.79 | **42.7%** |
| 4 — Habsiguda (original) | 50.03 | 77.03 | **35.1%** |
| 5 — Habsiguda (fine-tuned) | 55.34 | 77.03 | **28.2%** |

### Phase Change Behavior

| Stage | RL Phase Changes | Baseline Phase Changes | Ratio |
|-------|----------------:|----------------------:|-------|
| 2 — Multi-Head DQN (single) | 252.9 | 109.0 | 2.32× |
| 4 — Habsiguda (original) | 705.2 | 450.0 | 1.57× |
| 5 — Habsiguda (fine-tuned) | 553.2 | 450.0 | 1.23× |

> [!TIP]
> The fine-tuning reduced excessive phase switching from 1.57× to 1.23× the baseline, thanks to the increased phase change penalty (-1.0 vs -0.05) and higher minimum green time (20s vs 10s).

### Fine-Tuning Impact (Stage 4 → Stage 5)

| Metric | Stage 4 (Original) | Stage 5 (Fine-Tuned) | Improvement |
|--------|-------------------:|--------------------:|-------------|
| **Throughput** | 633.3 veh/h | 824.4 veh/h | **+30.2%** |
| **Waiting Time** | 1.57 s | 1.86 s | -18.5% (trade-off) |
| **Queue Length** | 50.03 | 55.34 | -10.6% (trade-off) |
| **Phase Changes** | 705.2 | 553.2 | **-21.6% ↓** |
| **Avg Speed** | — | 7.67 m/s | +5.1% vs baseline |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Fine-tuning recovered 30.2% of throughput while dramatically reducing unnecessary phase switching. The slight increase in waiting time and queue length is a deliberate trade-off — the higher minimum green time (20s) means the agent keeps phases longer, allowing more vehicles to clear but briefly increasing waits for cross-traffic.

---

## Evolution Summary

```mermaid
graph LR
    S1["Stage 1<br/>Basic DQN<br/>1 intersection<br/>Proof of concept"] --> S2["Stage 2<br/>Multi-Head DQN<br/>1 intersection<br/>73.9% wait ↓"]
    S2 --> S3["Stage 3<br/>Grid Network<br/>9 intersections<br/>Multi-agent"]
    S3 --> S4["Stage 4<br/>Habsiguda Corridor<br/>6 real junctions<br/>Transfer learning"]
    S4 --> S5["Stage 5<br/>Fine-Tuned<br/>+30% throughput<br/>Optimized penalties"]

    style S1 fill:#95a5a6,stroke:#7f8c8d,color:#fff
    style S2 fill:#3498db,stroke:#2980b9,color:#fff
    style S3 fill:#2ecc71,stroke:#27ae60,color:#fff
    style S4 fill:#f39c12,stroke:#e67e22,color:#fff
    style S5 fill:#e74c3c,stroke:#c0392b,color:#fff
```

| Milestone | What Changed | Key Achievement |
|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| Stage 1 → 2 | DQN → Multi-Head DQN with regime classifier | 73.9% waiting time reduction |
| Stage 2 → 3 | Single intersection → 9-junction grid | Multi-agent scalability proven |
| Stage 3 → 4 | Synthetic grid → Real-world Habsiguda corridor | Transfer learning demonstrated |
| Stage 4 → 5 | Raw transfer → Fine-tuned penalties & min green | 30.2% throughput recovery, 21.6% fewer switches |
